Hello all,

We have a funded (UK/EU) PhD opportunity at the Diabetes Research Centre, University of Leicester, for a student to use accelerometer data to look at physical activity/movement patterns indicative of pre-frailty and frailty. The project would suit an enthusiastic student with a background in Data Science and a strong interest in health and lifestyle.

The student would gain skills in accelerometry, signal processing, statistics, and epidemiology. The project benefits from a multi-disciplinary collaboration between researchers with expertise in lifestyle, accelerometery, engineering and frailty.

Details available at either of the links below:

Find a PhD - accelerometer and frailty <https://www.findaphd.com/phds/project/identification-of-movement-patterns-indicative-of-frailty-and-pre-frailty-using-wearable-activity-monitors/?p107915>

Leicester PhD - accelerometer and frailty <https://www2.le.ac.uk/research-degrees/funding/life-sciences>

Please feel free to contact me if you have any queries or would like any further information (alex.r...@leicester.ac.uk),

Alex Rowlands

